<title>SWEDEN: Swedish HUI sees GDP 2.1 pct '97, CPI 0.5 pct '97.</title>
<headline>Swedish HUI sees GDP 2.1 pct '97, CPI 0.5 pct '97.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Retail and Wholesale Institute (HUI) on Monday forecast the Consumer Price index increasing 0.5 percent in 1997 and 1.5 percent in 1998.</p>
<p>In its latest forecast, HUI also forecast Gross Domestic Product (GDP) rising 2.1 percent in 1997 and 3.0 percent in 1998.  </p>
<p>Following is a list of HUI's latest forecasts with changes in percentage points.</p>
<p>					 1997	 1998</p>
<p> Consumer Price Index	     0.5	  1.5</p>
<p> Industrial production	    4.0	  5.0</p>
<p> Unemployment, level		8.4	  7.8</p>
<p> Current account (Bln SKR)     50.0	 56.0</p>
<p> Trade balance (Bln SKR)	131.0	141.0</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	   2.1	  3.0</p>
<p> Private consumption		2.0	  2.5</p>
<p> Public consumption		-0.5	 -0.2</p>
<p> Export				 5.0	  6.0</p>
<p> Import				 4.0	  6.0</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
